.TH BTWCTL 1 "November 2026" "btwctl" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
btwctl \- control the Creative BT\-W5 and BT\-W6 Bluetooth audio dongles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B btwctl
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-\-notify ]
.RB [ \-\-device
.IR VID:PID ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B btwctl
changes the settings of a Creative BT\-W5 or BT\-W6 USB Bluetooth audio dongle: the aptX Adaptive
mode, the headset microphone (HFP), pairing and switching between headsets. It can also apply
settings automatically: per\-headset preferences, Low Latency while a game runs, and making the
dongle the default audio device while a headset is connected.
.PP
The dongle is found automatically. Sound itself needs no tool: the dongle is a standard USB sound
card, and volume is set from the desktop as usual.
.PP
.B btwctl gui
opens a settings window,
.B btwctl tray
a system tray icon. Before version 0.7 the program was called
.BR btw5\-switch ,
which still works as a command name.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Also show the raw USB traffic.
.TP
.B \-\-notify
Show the result as a desktop notification, for keyboard shortcuts and launchers.
.TP
.BI \-\-device " VID:PID"
Use the dongle with this USB ID (for example
.BR 041e:3130 ),
to try other Creative dongles. Also set by the
.B BTW5_DEVICE
environment variable.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Status
.TP
.BR status " [" \-\-json ]
Connected headset, aptX mode, microphone and automatic microphone switching.
.TP
.BR info " [" \-\-json ]
Dongle model, firmware version and serial number.
.TP
.BR paired " [" \-\-json "] [" \-\-names ]
The 4 pairing slots.
.TP
.BR dump " [" \-\-json ]
Every readable register, for bug reports. Read\-only.
.SS Settings
.TP
.BR ll ", " hq ", " toggle
aptX Adaptive Low Latency, High Quality, or switch between the two. Needs a connected aptX Adaptive
headset.
.TP
.BR hfp " on|off"
Headset microphone (HFP). The dongle reconnects, so audio drops for a few seconds.
.TP
.BR auto\-hfp " on|off"
Switch to the microphone automatically when an application uses it.
.SS Headsets
.TP
.BR scan " [\fIseconds\fR] [" \-\-json ]
Disconnect the current headset and list nearby headsets in pairing mode (default 15 seconds). The
dongle often connects to a headset in pairing mode by itself; scan then says so.
.TP
.BI pair " headset" \fR\ [\fB\-\-timeout \fIseconds\fR]
Connect to a headset: an address shown by
.B scan
or (part of) the name of a paired headset.
.TP
.B disconnect
Disconnect the current headset.
.TP
.BR forget " [" \-y ]
Forget all paired headsets (asks first unless
.BR \-y ).
.SS Automation
These are applied by the background service
.RB ( "btwctl monitor" ,
see
.BR FILES ).
.TP
.BR prefer " [\fIheadset\fR] [" \-\-aptx " hq|ll] [" \-\-hfp " on|off] [" \-\-auto\-hfp " on|off] [" \-\-current "] [" \-\-clear ]
Settings to apply whenever that headset connects. Without arguments, list them.
.I headset
can be
.B current
for the connected one;
.B \-\-current
remembers its current settings.
.TP
.BR game\-mode " [status|on|off|add \fIword\fR|remove \fIword\fR]"
Use Low Latency while a game runs. A process counts as a game if its command line contains one of
the listed words (Steam, gamescope, Lutris and Heroic games by default).
.TP
.BR audio\-follow " [status|on|off]"
Make the dongle the default audio output (and, with HFP on, microphone) while a headset is
connected, and switch back afterwards. Uses PipeWire.
.SS Programs
.TP
.B gui
Settings window (needs PyQt6 or PySide6).
.TP
.BR tray " [" \-\-interval " \fIseconds\fR]"
System tray icon.
.TP
.BR monitor " [" \-\-notify "] [" \-\-all "] [" \-\-no\-reconnect "] [" \-\-no\-automation ]
Print headset and setting changes as they happen, show notifications with
.BR \-\-notify ,
and apply the automation above. While it runs, it shares the dongle with other btwctl commands.
.TP
.BR waybar " [" \-\-interval " \fIseconds\fR]"
Status as JSON for a waybar or polybar module.
.TP
.BI raw " byte..." \fR\ [\fB\-\-listen \fIseconds\fR]
Send a raw command and print the replies (protocol exploration).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/btwctl/config.ini
Per\-headset preferences, game mode and audio\-follow settings.
.TP
.I btwctl\-monitor.service
The background service (systemd user unit). Start it with
.BR "systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now btwctl\-monitor.service" .
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/70\-btwctl.rules
Gives the logged\-in user access to the dongle. Unplug and replug the dongle after installing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BTW5_DEVICE
USB ID of the dongle, like
.BR \-\-device .
.TP
.BR LANGUAGE ", " LANG
Language of the window and tray, if translated.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
btwctl status
btwctl ll
btwctl pair momentum
btwctl prefer current \-\-current
btwctl game\-mode on
btwctl \-\-notify toggle        # for a keyboard shortcut
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wpctl (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
https://github.com/doodersrage/btwctl
